{
    // FI_Standard_LendOffer.ergo - the lender's offer (a yield-curve bid) for FI bonds
    // Author: CannonQ (2026)
    //
    // Holds a lender's capital and buys FI_Standard_Bond units that clear a simple-interest yield
    // the lender sets per maturity: new ones, by filling an FI_Standard_Order, and existing ones,
    // from any ask that follows the ask convention below (ZC_Standard_SaleOrder, or a later one).
    // Any batcher matches the offer, for the fee the offer itself sets, and the bond unit is
    // delivered to the owner script.
    // It is ZC_Standard_LendOffer read against the FI bond's registers, with the lender's bounds
    // on the coupon schedule in R7. It buys whole bond units only, never shares, and refuses an
    // owner equal to this market's share mint. Nothing here touches coupons: the bond pays them
    // into its own coupon pool.
    //
    // CONSTANTS (one offer address per repayment asset, under one shared template)
    // CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN: Coll[Byte] - the asset lent and repaid; EMPTY for ERG
    // CONST_ORDER_HASH: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of the FI_Standard_Order tree for that asset
    // CONST_BOND_HASH: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of the FI_Standard_Bond tree for that asset
    // CONST_MINT_HASH: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of the FI_Standard_FractionalMint tree for that
    //   asset; the owner hash R4 may not equal it
    // There is no priced-order hash. No ask script is pinned.
    // Deploy-time couplings: CONST_ORDER_HASH must name the order compiled with this
    // CONST_BOND_HASH and CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN (only an existing bond is checked against
    // CONST_BOND_HASH here); CONST_MINT_HASH must come from the mint as finally compiled.
    //
    // CAPITAL
    // ERG offer: the box value, no tokens. Token offer: tokens(0) = (repayment token, amount), and
    // the box value pays fees and box minimums.
    //
    // REGISTERS (R4 to R7, all present; a fill's continuation copies R4, R5, R7, resets R6, has
    // no R8 or later register and is created at HEIGHT - 999 or later)
    // R4: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of the owner script: may cancel, receives the bond unit
    // R5: Coll[Long] - terms, at ZC_Standard_LendOffer's indices: 11 for ERG or 15 for a token
    //   offer, then the yield curve.
    //   0 minimum yield, basis points of simple interest per 262800 blocks (one year of 2-minute
    //     blocks), >= 0. The yield required at any maturity is never below it. With no curve
    //     points it is the offer's one yield at every maturity.
    //   1 minimum and 2 maximum blocks left to maturity
    //   3 ERG batcher fee per fill, and expiry refund fee for either market, nanoERG. A fill
    //     needs at least 100000000 (0.1 ERG); an offer below it never fills, and its owner cancels
    //     it or anyone refunds it after expiry.
    //   4 lender fee reserve to put in a NEW bond (bond R9(0)), nanoERG, exact; the FI order
    //     refuses a bond born with less than 100000000
    //   5 collateral floor in basis points of the repayment, and 8 maximum oracle age in
    //     blocks: read only by the collateral policy expression
    //   6 expiry height; fills require HEIGHT < expiry, and from then on anyone may refund
    //   7 minimum price of one fill, in raw units of the repayment asset (see LIMITS for small
    //     loans)
    //   9 and 10 are not read (in ZC_Standard_LendOffer they bound share purchases)
    //   Token offers additionally commit (unchanged through every continuation):
    //   11 original capital, raw token units, positive
    //   12 original total ERG spending budget, excluding 1000000 plus the expiry refund fee
    //   13 minimum fill, basis points of ORIGINAL capital, 100..10000 (at least 1%)
    //   14 original batcher reward budget, positive and below the total spending budget
    //   A token fill pays floor(R5(14) * price / R5(11)), never rounded up to the fee floor: a
    //   fee so calculated below 100000000 rejects the fill. Total ERG outflow, including box
    //   funding and new-bond reserve, is at most floor(R5(12) * price / R5(11)). Splitting cannot
    //   increase either allowance. The continuation retains 1000000 plus the expiry refund fee.
    //   Then the yield curve, from index 11 (ERG) or 15 (token): 0 to 20 points, each two values
    //   (yield bps, blocks left to maturity). Blocks left strictly increase from point to point.
    // R6: Coll[Byte] - policy hash (32 bytes), optionally followed by the predecessor offer id
    //   (32 bytes). Every fill's continuation must set that suffix to SELF.id. The policy is an
    //   expression supplied in context var 1 and run with this offer as SELF; it is the whole
    //   collateral decision. FI_Standard_ERG_SigUSD_CollateralPolicy is one: it reads R5(5) and
    //   R5(8), requires the bond's agreed liquidation expression, a covenant ratio R6(12) at or
    //   above the floor and an oracle age R6(14) at or above R5(8), and collateral worth, now, the
    //   floor plus a new bond's fee reserve plus (when the cover moves with the price) one Record
    //   bounty, and at least the bond's own ratio.
    // R7: Coll[Long] - bounds on the bond's coupon schedule, exactly 5 values:
    //   0 minimum coupon, raw units of the repayment asset: bond R6(7) >= it
    //   1 minimum coupon count, >= 1: bond R6(8) >= it. With no coupon there is no checkpoint,
    //     and the covenant is never tested.
    //   2 maximum gap in blocks between covenant tests: start to first due height (R6(9)), the
    //     period R6(10), and the last recordable checkpoint (below) to maturity must each be at
    //     most this. With no recordable checkpoint the gap is the bond's whole life.
    //   3 maximum grace: bond R6(11) <= it
    //   4 maximum cure window: bond R6(13) <= it
    //   Every bond bought here has the grace no longer than the period, R6(11) <= R6(10): the FI
    //   order requires it whenever there are coupons, and R7(1) >= 1 means there are. With one
    //   coupon the period still counts: it must lie between the grace and R7(2).
    //
    // RECORDABLE CHECKPOINTS
    // Checkpoint k is coupon k's due height, start + R6(9) + k * R6(10). The bond accepts Record
    // breach (opening a breach when its covenant expression finds the collateral below the
    // ratio) from a checkpoint to checkpoint + grace, only below maturity - 720, and not in its
    // quiet zone: the last max(2, min(720, grace / 2)) blocks before the next unpaid coupon's
    // miss height (due + grace). The last recordable checkpoint counted here is the last one
    // whose window closes by maturity - 721 (due + grace <= maturity - 721). The FI order gives
    // every covenant bond a grace of at least 30, so no quiet zone covers its due heights, and
    // puts the first due height at or after the fill, so each such checkpoint can be recorded
    // at its own due height unless the bond is liquidatable or a breach is already open. The
    // gaps R7(2) bounds are therefore the gaps between tests.
    //
    // THE YIELD CURVE
    // The yield required for a bond with D blocks left is the curve's yield at D, and never less
    // than R5(0). Between two neighbouring points it falls on the straight line joining them;
    // below the first point it is the first point's yield, above the last the last's. R5(1) and
    // R5(2) still decide which maturities are bought at all. With no points the yield is R5(0).
    // On a segment from (y1, D1) to (y2, D2) the yield is Y / L, with L = D2 - D1 and
    // Y = y1 * L + (y2 - y1) * (D - D1), so the test below multiplies through by L: no division,
    // no rounding. A flat yield has L = 1. A curve with points out of order is refused.
    //
    // THE YIELD TEST (for one whole bond unit)
    // Paying price P now for repayment R at maturity, with D blocks left, must satisfy
    //   R * 10000 * 262800 * L >= P * (10000 * 262800 * L + Y * D).
    // R is the bond's R6(0); coupons are not counted. D is the bond's maturity R9(2) less HEIGHT
    // and must be above 0. P is the principal of a new bond or what the seller's payout holds.
    // For an ERG offer P includes the batcher fee, so the yield is net of it; a token offer pays
    // that fee in nanoERG outside the test.
    //
    // CONTEXT VARS
    // 0 Int continuation index, or the refund index after expiry (every path but cancel). A fill
    // also needs 1 Coll[Byte] the collateral policy expression.
    // Buying from an ask also needs: 2 Int ask input index; 3 Int data-input index of the bond's
    // state box; 4 Coll[Byte] the serialized order box that minted the bond asset; 5 Int delivery
    // output index; 7 Int the seller's payout output index. The absence of var 2 selects a
    // new-bond fill, which also requires var 3 absent. Var 6 is not read.
    //
    // THE ASK CONVENTION (what this offer expects of the box at var 2, whatever its script)
    // tokens(0) is the token for sale. R4: Coll[Byte] is blake2b256 of the seller script. A fill
    // pays one payout box at the seller script with R4 = the ask's box id and R5: Long = the raw
    // units it pays for, holding the payment: its nanoERG for an ERG price, its tokens(0) for a
    // token price. The ask's own script must enforce that R5; ZC_Standard_SaleOrder does.
    // The offer's price is whatever that payout holds: it never reads the ask's price. It
    // requires the payout's R5 to be 1, the unit delivered here, and the payout to be neither
    // the continuation nor the delivery. Only one unit of a bond asset circulates (the bond
    // holds the other 2), so the ask cannot have sold more than that unit, and anything above
    // the ask's own price reaches the seller, not the batcher.
    //
    // NEW BOND (var 2 absent)
    // INPUTS(0) is an FI_Standard_Order (CONST_ORDER_HASH), whose own script validates the bond
    // at OUTPUTS(1) and pays the borrower at OUTPUTS(2). OUTPUTS(0) is the delivery. Checked
    // here: the order box was created fewer than 1051200 blocks before HEIGHT (an older box can
    // be spent under storage rent without its script running), the bond asset is the order's
    // id, the delivery holds 1 unit of it, the bond's principal is this offer's asset, and the
    // bond's fee reserve R9(0) equals R5(4). That order only lends in the repayment asset alone
    // (a token loan carries at most 1000000 nanoERG beside it), so the principal is the price
    // with no further check: bond R6(1) nanoERG for ERG, the amount of the R7 principal token for
    // a token.
    //
    // EXISTING BOND (var 2 present)
    // The ask sells one unit of asset X and is paid through its payout.
    // Origin: var 4 hashes to X, so it is the box whose spending minted X, its script is the
    //   FI order, and it was created fewer than 1051200 blocks before HEIGHT. Since it was spent
    //   before HEIGHT, its script ran, which proves X was minted by the order's rules: supply 3,
    //   2 locked in the bond. So an offer cannot buy a bond whose origin order is 1051200 or more
    //   blocks old.
    // State: the data input holds 2 units of X under CONST_BOND_HASH, so it is the live bond and
    //   its registers are the terms; its principal must be this offer's asset. A settled bond (the
    //   vault holds the 2 units) is not bought.
    // Not liquidatable, as the bond counts it: at least as many coupons paid, R9(3), as missed
    //   (coupon k is missed from its due height plus the grace), and no open breach at or past
    //   its deadline R9(5). Maturity is excluded by the yield test's D > 0.
    // No fee reserve leaves the offer on this path.
    //
    // DELIVERY
    // A box at the owner script holding only (X, 1), at least 1000000 nanoERG, R7 = SELF.id,
    // created at HEIGHT - 999 or later. The owner hash may not be CONST_MINT_HASH.
    // On a new-bond fill it is OUTPUTS(0), which the FI order also requires to carry the EIP-4
    // name and description in R4 and R5 and the decimals "0" in R6.
    //
    // WHAT MAY LEAVE THE BOX
    // The price, the batcher fee, the delivery funding, a new bond's fee reserve, and at most
    // 1000000 nanoERG of box minimum on a token offer. Everything else stays in the continuation.
    // The delivery and continuation are tagged with SELF.id, so independent offers may fill in
    // one transaction. Neither output can satisfy another offer. Additional inputs and
    // independent matches are allowed.
    //
    // EXPIRY REFUND (anyone, once HEIGHT >= R5(6))
    // Var 0 names the refund: at the owner script, R4 = this box's id, no R5, created at
    // HEIGHT - 999 or later, every token of this box, and at least this value less R5(3). It
    // reads only R4 and R5 (whose length must still be valid), so it works whatever R6 and R7
    // hold. Several offers may be refunded in one
    // transaction, each to its own tagged output.
    //
    // CANCEL
    // Any other input whose script hashes to R4, created fewer than 1051200 blocks before HEIGHT
    // (an older box can be spent under storage rent without its script running), releases this
    // box at any height, unchecked.
    //
    // OWNER SCRIPTS
    // The owner script must be one that only its owner can spend in every instance: P2PK,
    // multisig, or a contract whose keys are compiled-in constants. Anyone can create a box at a
    // script that reads its authority from its own registers, so naming one lets anyone cancel
    // this offer and take everything it holds, and take a delivery, whose registers other than
    // R7 the batcher writes. FI_Standard_FractionalMint and FI_Standard_FractionalVault can be
    // instantiated by anyone and must never be the owner hash. Builders should refuse any other
    // kind of owner script.
    //
    // LIMITS
    // - Best execution is not enforced. The offer never does worse than its terms, but a batcher
    //   chooses which ask it meets.
    // - The covenant is tested at coupon checkpoints only: R7(2) bounds the gap between tests,
    //   not how far the collateral can fall within one.
    // - The bounds apply to the schedule as written: an existing bond is judged on its whole
    //   coupon count, whatever it has already paid, and its coupons are not counted in the yield.
    // - Settled bonds and shares are not bought: only whole units of a live bond.
    // - A fill always leaves a continuation; dust left in it comes back by cancelling or at expiry.
    // - A purchase is judged at the payout's whole value. One priced below the minimum box value
    //   in nanoERG is therefore judged at that minimum.
    // - No bond whose origin order is 1051200 or more blocks old can be bought, new or existing.
    // - Small loans whose cover moves with the oracle price: one recorded breach takes up to
    //   0.5 ERG from the collateral, so the lender can be left with less than the repayment when
    //   (ratio - 100%) x repayment is under 0.5 ERG. The protection is the minimum fill R5(7):
    //   keep it above 0.5 ERG / (floor - 100%) worth of the repayment asset (about 1.67 ERG at
    //   a 130% floor, 1 ERG at 150%).
    //   That bounds the repayment only. To stay whole on the fee reserve R5(4) as well when someone
    //   else liquidates, use (0.5 ERG + R5(4)) / (floor - 100%), plus the batcher fee on a token
    //   offer. On a SigUSD offer convert at the highest ERG price expected before the expiry.
    // - A bond's 0.01 ERG Refresh bounty is paid only from maturity on; on a bond box older than
    //   525600 blocks it can be taken in the maturity block, outside the policy's allowance.
    // - The collateral policy values collateral at one oracle pool box; see
    //   FI_Standard_ERG_SigUSD_CollateralPolicy.
    // - This box has no refresh path. Left 1051200 blocks it can be spent under storage rent,
    //   and taken whole if its value does not cover the fee; set the expiry well before that.

    val ownerHash = SELF.R4[Coll[Byte]].get
    val ownerAuth = INPUTS.exists { (b: Box) =>
        b.id != SELF.id && blake2b256(b.propositionBytes) == ownerHash &&
        b.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1051200
    }

    if (ownerAuth) {
        sigmaProp(true)
    } else {
        val terms = SELF.R5[Coll[Long]].get
        val nextIndex = getVar[Int](0).get
        // Taken from the box so the compiler cannot fold the constant into the template.
        val lendsERG = CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN == SELF.id.slice(0, 0)
        // Where the yield curve starts: after the fixed terms of this market.
        val base = if (lendsERG) 11 else 15

        if (terms.size < base || terms.size > base + 40 || (terms.size - base) % 2 != 0 ||
            nextIndex < 0 || nextIndex >= OUTPUTS.size) {
            sigmaProp(false)
        } else if (HEIGHT.toLong >= terms(6)) {
            // Expiry refund, by anyone: everything goes back to the owner, less the fee R5(3).
            val refund = OUTPUTS(nextIndex)
            sigmaProp(
                blake2b256(refund.propositionBytes) == ownerHash &&
                refund.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id &&
                refund.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1000 &&
                refund.R5[Coll[Byte]].isDefined == false &&
                refund.tokens == SELF.tokens &&
                refund.value >= SELF.value - terms(3)
            )
        } else {
            // R6 and R7 are read only here, so a box with either malformed still refunds.
            val bounds = SELF.R7[Coll[Long]].get
            val policyRecord = SELF.R6[Coll[Byte]].get
            val policyHash = policyRecord.slice(0, 32)
            if ((policyRecord.size != 32 && policyRecord.size != 64) || bounds.size != 5) {
                sigmaProp(false)
            } else {
                val next = OUTPUTS(nextIndex)
                val saleIndex = getVar[Int](2)
                val primary = !saleIndex.isDefined

                val bond = if (primary) OUTPUTS(1) else CONTEXT.dataInputs(getVar[Int](3).get)
                val unit = if (primary) OUTPUTS(0) else OUTPUTS(getVar[Int](5).get)
                val asset = bond.tokens(0)._1
                val borrower = bond.R6[Coll[Long]].get
                val lender = bond.R9[Coll[Long]].get
                val principalTokens = bond.R7[Coll[(Coll[Byte], Long)]].get
                // The token delivered and how many raw units of it: exactly 1 bond unit.
                val traded = unit.tokens(0)._1
                val units = unit.tokens(0)._2

                // What the offer pays, in raw units of the repayment asset.
                val price = if (primary) {
                    if (lendsERG) borrower(1) else principalTokens(0)._2
                } else {
                    // Whatever the seller's payout holds. The ask's own price is never read.
                    val payout = OUTPUTS(getVar[Int](7).get)
                    if (lendsERG) {
                        payout.value
                    } else if (payout.tokens.size > 0 && payout.tokens(0)._1 == CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN) {
                        payout.tokens(0)._2
                    } else 0L
                }

                val batcherFee = if (lendsERG) terms(3)
                    else if (terms(11) > 0L && terms(14) > 0L && price > 0L && price <= terms(11)) {
                        (terms(14).toBigInt * price.toBigInt / terms(11).toBigInt).toLong
                    } else 0L

                val sourceValid = if (primary) {
                    // The order lends in the repayment asset alone, so its principal is the price.
                    val order = INPUTS(0)
                    !(getVar[Int](3).isDefined) &&
                    blake2b256(order.propositionBytes) == CONST_ORDER_HASH &&
                    HEIGHT.toLong - order.creationInfo._1.toLong < 1051200L &&
                    asset == order.id && traded == asset && units == 1L &&
                    (if (lendsERG) principalTokens.size == 0
                        else principalTokens.size == 1 && principalTokens.forall { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                            t._1 == CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN
                        }) &&
                    lender(0) == terms(4)
                } else {
                    val sale = INPUTS(saleIndex.get)
                    val payoutIndex = getVar[Int](7).get
                    val payout = OUTPUTS(payoutIndex)
                    val originBytes = getVar[Coll[Byte]](4).get
                    val origin = Global.deserializeTo[Box](originBytes)
                    // The ask convention. No ask script is pinned: the payout goes to the seller
                    // the ask names, is tagged with the ask, and pays for exactly the unit
                    // delivered. Then the origin order, the live state box, and the bond's own
                    // liquidatable test.
                    sale.id != SELF.id &&
                    sale.tokens.size > 0 && sale.tokens(0)._1 == traded &&
                    traded == asset && units == 1L &&
                    blake2b256(payout.propositionBytes) == sale.R4[Coll[Byte]].get &&
                    payout.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == sale.id &&
                    payout.R5[Long].get == units &&
                    payoutIndex != nextIndex && payoutIndex != getVar[Int](5).get &&
                    blake2b256(originBytes) == asset &&
                    blake2b256(origin.propositionBytes) == CONST_ORDER_HASH &&
                    HEIGHT.toLong - origin.creationInfo._1.toLong < 1051200L &&
                    blake2b256(bond.propositionBytes) == CONST_BOND_HASH &&
                    (if (lendsERG) principalTokens.size == 0
                        else principalTokens.size == 1 && principalTokens.forall { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                            t._1 == CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN
                        }) &&
                    bond.tokens(0)._2 == 2L &&
                    // Not liquidatable, as the bond counts it: at least as many coupons paid as
                    // missed, and no open breach at or past its deadline.
                    lender(3) >= (if (HEIGHT.toLong < lender(1) + borrower(9) + borrower(11)) 0L
                        else min(borrower(8), (HEIGHT.toLong - lender(1) - borrower(9) - borrower(11)) / borrower(10) + 1L)) &&
                    (lender(5) == 0L || HEIGHT.toLong < lender(5))
                }

                // The schedule, as the bond counts it, inside the lender's bounds. The bond is one
                // the FI order created, which keeps its terms in the bond's clamps and every
                // coupon due before maturity, so nothing here overflows or divides by zero.
                val count = borrower(8)
                val period = borrower(10)
                val firstDue = lender(1) + borrower(9)
                // The last checkpoint whose window (due + grace) closes by maturity - 721 is the
                // last counted as tested; with the grace no longer than the period (the FI order's
                // rule) it can be recorded at its due height. With none, the gap runs from start.
                val recordable = lender(2) - 721L - firstDue - borrower(11)
                val lastTested = if (recordable < 0L) lender(1)
                    else firstDue + min(count - 1L, recordable / period) * period
                val scheduleValid =
                    bounds(1) >= 1L && count >= bounds(1) && borrower(7) >= bounds(0) &&
                    borrower(9) <= bounds(2) && period <= bounds(2) && lender(2) - lastTested <= bounds(2) &&
                    borrower(11) <= bounds(3) && borrower(13) <= bounds(4)

                // Fills run only before the expiry, R5(6); from then on this box can only be
                // refunded or cancelled.
                val remaining = lender(2) - HEIGHT.toLong
                val year = 2628000000L.toBigInt // 10000 basis points * 262800 blocks
                val cost = if (lendsERG) price + batcherFee else price

                // The yield curve: points of (yield bps, blocks left) after the fixed terms.
                val curve = terms.slice(base, terms.size)
                val points = curve.size / 2
                // Blocks left strictly increase from point to point (odd positions hold them).
                val ordered = curve.indices.forall { (j: Int) => j % 2 == 0 || j < 3 || curve(j) > curve(j - 2) }
                // How many points lie at or below the bond's blocks left: the segment it falls on.
                val below = curve.indices.filter { (j: Int) => j % 2 == 1 && curve(j) <= remaining }.size
                val flat = points == 0 || below == 0 || below == points
                // The required yield as rate / span, exactly. Flat ends and an empty curve have
                // span 1.
                val span = if (flat) 1L.toBigInt else (curve(2 * below + 1) - curve(2 * below - 1)).toBigInt
                val rate = if (points == 0) {
                    terms(0).toBigInt
                } else if (below == 0) {
                    curve(0).toBigInt
                } else if (below == points) {
                    curve(curve.size - 2).toBigInt
                } else {
                    val low = 2 * (below - 1)
                    curve(low).toBigInt * span +
                        (curve(low + 2).toBigInt - curve(low).toBigInt) * (remaining - curve(low + 1)).toBigInt
                }
                val floorRate = terms(0).toBigInt * span
                val required = if (rate < floorRate) floorRate else rate

                val termsValid =
                    terms(0) >= 0L && batcherFee >= 100000000L && ordered &&
                    remaining > 0L && remaining >= terms(1) && remaining <= terms(2) &&
                    price > 0L && price >= terms(7) &&
                    borrower(0).toBigInt * year * span >=
                        cost.toBigInt * (year * span + required * remaining.toBigInt)

                // The unit goes straight to the owner script, tagged with this offer's id.
                val delivered =
                    unit.tokens.size == 1 && unit.value >= 1000000L &&
                    unit.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1000 &&
                    blake2b256(unit.propositionBytes) == ownerHash && ownerHash != CONST_MINT_HASH &&
                    unit.R7[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id

                // nanoERG that may leave: fee, delivery, a new bond's reserve, and either the ERG
                // price or the box minimum that rides with a token payment.
                val reserve = if (primary) lender(0) else 0L
                val ergBesidePrice = if (lendsERG) price else if (primary) borrower(1) else 1000000L
                val ergOut = batcherFee + 1000000L + reserve + ergBesidePrice
                val capitalKept = if (lendsERG) {
                    next.tokens.size == 0 && SELF.tokens.size == 0 &&
                    next.value >= SELF.value - ergOut
                } else {
                    val have = if (SELF.tokens.size == 1 && SELF.tokens(0)._1 == CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN) {
                        SELF.tokens(0)._2
                    } else 0L
                    val left = have - price
                    val original = terms(11)
                    val budget = terms(12)
                    val minPercent = terms(13)
                    original > 0L && have <= original && budget > 0L &&
                    terms(3) >= 100000000L && terms(14) > 0L && terms(14) < budget &&
                    minPercent >= 100L && minPercent <= 10000L &&
                    price.toBigInt * 10000L.toBigInt >= original.toBigInt * minPercent.toBigInt &&
                    (SELF.value.toBigInt - next.value.toBigInt) * original.toBigInt <= budget.toBigInt * price.toBigInt &&
                    next.value.toBigInt >= 1000000L.toBigInt + terms(3).toBigInt &&
                    left >= 0L &&
                    next.value >= SELF.value - ergOut &&
                    (if (left == 0L) next.tokens.size == 0
                     else next.tokens.size == 1 && next.tokens(0)._1 == CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN &&
                          next.tokens(0)._2 == left)
                }

                val continued =
                    next.propositionBytes == SELF.propositionBytes &&
                    next.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1000 &&
                    next.R8[Coll[Byte]].isDefined == false &&
                    next.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == ownerHash &&
                    next.R5[Coll[Long]].get == terms &&
                    next.R6[Coll[Byte]].get == policyHash ++ SELF.id &&
                    next.R7[Coll[Long]].get == bounds

                // The policy in var 1 must hash to R6's first 32 bytes; it runs with this box
                // as SELF.
                val policyAgreed = blake2b256(getVar[Coll[Byte]](1).get) == policyHash

                sigmaProp(
                    sourceValid && scheduleValid && termsValid && delivered && capitalKept &&
                    continued && policyAgreed
                ) && executeFromVar[SigmaProp](1)
            }
        }
    }
}
